  {
   "heading": "Proposals for new districts",
   "text": "Demands for the administrative bifurcation and reorganization of existing districts in Maharashtra are driven by the challenges of governing extensive geographical territories and managing high-density urban populations. In 2015, public representatives and former ministers formally petitioned for the creation of several districts to support rural and tribal blocks, including Katol, Chimur, Pusad, Khamgaon, Achalpur, and Aheri.\nSubsequently, in 2018, the state government under then Chief Minister Devendra Fadnavis constituted a high-level committee led by the Chief Secretary to systematically evaluate these needs. The committee submitted a structural proposal to create 22 new districts across the state to streamline public utility delivery and optimize regional governance.",
